# The browsers this app promises to work in.
#
# `[production]` is the truthful minimum: the versions the app already needs, and not one
# step higher. Two CSS features set it, both of them load-bearing rather than decorative:
#
#   light-dark()  Chrome 123 · Firefox 120 · Safari 17.5 · Samsung 27
#                 52 uses in `app/ui/tokens.ts` — the entire semantic colour layer. Below
#                 this every one of them is invalid and the colour falls back to inherited.
#   pow()         Chrome 120 · Firefox 118 · Safari 15.4
#                 9 uses in `app/ui/tokens.ts` — every step of the app's type scale except
#                 `md`, which is `1rem` itself. Written as
#                 `calc(1rem * pow(var(--type-scale-ratio), n))` so that changing a ratio
#                 recomputes the row rather than leaving thirty stale literals behind.
#
# `light-dark()` is therefore the binding one, and **Safari is the binding browser**: it
# ships with macOS and cannot be updated on its own, so raising this line is not asking
# somebody to update a browser, it is asking them to update their computer. That is the
# reason this floor is the minimum rather than something roomier — a promise that is
# already untrue on the day it is written is worse than no promise, and one that is
# needlessly high locks people out for a feature nobody used yet.
#
# `[development]` is our own machines, so it may as well be the newest thing; `not dead`
# is not optional there, because `last 1 version` on its own still answers `ie 11`.
#
# Nothing enforces the CSS floor. The stylesheet never passes through a build step —
# `css()` emits it during SSR and `tokens.ts` is a template string — so `light-dark()` and
# `pow()` are kept by reading, not by tooling. The one place a version does bite is the
# islands' JavaScript, which `app/browser-support.ts` compiles against the production
# floor below, in development too: what gets tested should be what ships.

[production]
chrome >= 123
edge >= 123
firefox >= 120
safari >= 17.5
ios_saf >= 17.5
samsung >= 27

[development]
last 1 version
not dead
